  "sections": {
    "1": {
      "purpose": "Purpose: This System Requirement Specification (SRS) defines the system-level requirements for the telemetry acquisition subsystem of [Project Name]. The purpose of this software is to acquire and process real-time telemetry data from various sensor channels, enabling critical mission operations in a defense environment.  The system will support existing parent systems by providing reliable and timely access to critical operational data. This SRS is intended for use by developers, engineers, testers, and other stakeholders involved in the development and deployment of this software.",
      "scope": "This System Requirement Specification (SRS) defines the system-level requirements for the telemetry acquisition subsystem of the [Project Name] R&D software project.  The purpose of this software is to acquire and process real-time telemetry data from various sensor channels, enabling critical mission operations in a defense environment. The system will support existing parent systems by providing reliable and timely access to critical operational data.\n\nScope:\n\nIn Scope:\n    * Acquisition and processing of telemetry data from at least three sensor channels simultaneously.\n    * Timestamping every acquired sample with a system time reference accurate to +/- 1 ms.\n    * Buffering at least 10,000 samples per channel before flow control is applied.\n    * Exposing acquired samples through a REST interface to the ground segment.\n    * Recording an engineering log with a minimum depth of 6 months of mission operations.\nOut of Scope:  This SRS does not define the detailed design or implementation of the telemetry acquisition subsystem, including specific sensor types, data processing algorithms, or REST API implementation details.\n\nNote: Detailed design information is provided in the System Design Document (SDD).",
