    "2": {
      "design_approach": "System Design Overview\n\nDesign Approach: This system is designed to acquire, timestamp, buffer, and transmit telemetry data from at least three sensor channels simultaneously.  The system interfaces with the ground segment via a REST interface for data transfer and analysis.  A detailed engineering log of mission operations will be maintained for at least six months.\n\nKey Architectural Components:\n\nSensor Acquisition Module: Acquires telemetry data from multiple sensor channels.\nData Buffering Module: Buffers acquired samples before flow control to maintain real-time data delivery.\nTimestamping Module: Timestamps each acquired sample with high accuracy.\nREST Interface Module: Exposes acquired data through a REST interface for ground segment access.\nEngineering Log Module: Records an engineering log of mission operations, maintaining at least six months of historical data.\n\nSystem Boundaries and Interfaces:\n\nGround Segment: The system exposes acquired samples through a REST interface to the ground segment for data transfer and analysis.\nEngineering Log:  The system maintains an engineering log with a minimum depth of six months of mission operation data, serving as a historical record for troubleshooting and operational analysis.\nPower Management Module: Operates within a 28 V DC power envelope not exceeding 45 W to ensure efficient power consumption and reliable operation.\n\nPerformance Requirements:\n\nSample Ingestion Rate: The system achieves a sample ingestion rate of at least 100 Hz per channel, enabling real-time data processing and analysis.\nMean Time Between Failures (MTBF):  The system's MTBF must be not less than 2000 hours to ensure continuous operation and minimize downtime.\n\nNon-Functional Requirements:\n\nData Integrity: The system operates within a controlled environment with defined boundaries to ensure data integrity and security. Access to acquisition controls is restricted to authenticated operators only, preventing unauthorized manipulation of the system.\nPower Consumption:  The system operates within a 28 V DC power envelope not exceeding 45 W, ensuring efficient power consumption and reliable operation.\n\nNote: Detailed design information regarding specific functionalities and interactions will be provided in subsequent sections of this specification.",
