      "data_structures": "Interface Design - Shared Data Structures\n\nThis section outlines the design of shared data structures used by the ground segment and sensor interfaces.\n\nData Structure Requirements:\n\nTelemetry Sample Envelopes: The ground segment interface will transmit telemetry sample envelopes as defined in api.proto (message TelemetrySample). This message structure will include channel information, timestamp, and a list of values representing the measured data.\n    * REQ-0101: The ground segment interface shall transmit telemetry sample envelopes as defined in api.proto (message TelemetrySample).\nAcquisition Command: The acquisition command interface will accept a StartCommand message to initiate the acquisition process. This message includes channel information and sample rate.\n    * REQ-0102: The acquisition command interface shall accept a StartCommand message to begin acquisition.\nHealth Report: The health reporting interface will expose an MTBF estimate as defined in api.proto (message HealthReport). This report provides information about the sensor's operational status and estimated Mean Time Between Failures.\n    * REQ-0103: The health reporting interface shall expose an MTBF estimate as defined in api.proto (message HealthReport).\n\nData Structure Implementation:\n\nThe implementation of these data structures will be based on the following considerations:\n\nSerialization: Data structures will be serialized to and from messages using a format compatible with the protocol specified in api.proto.\nSynchronization:  Shared data structures will be synchronized between the ground segment and sensor interfaces to ensure consistency and avoid race conditions.\n\nNote: This document is intended as a high-level overview of shared data structure design. Further details on implementation, including specific data structure definitions and synchronization mechanisms, will be provided in subsequent documents."
    },
